{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-vertex-operator-affine-coordinate","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:vertex-operator-affine-coordinate","kind":"remark","title":"The vertex-operator variable as the affine coordinate on $\\mathcal{S}_p$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-vertex-operator","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-contact-affine-chart"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-vertex-operator","tags":["vertex-operator","exceptional-divisor","contact-affine-chart"],"text":"vertex-operator-affine-coordinate.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:vertex-operator-affine-coordinate\"></a><p>In the QOU, the formal variable <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z</code> of the <a href=\"#def:vertex-operator\">vertex operator</a> algebra is the affine coordinate <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z = v_1/v_2</code> on the projective line <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_p</code>. This matches the contact affine coordinate <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Z = \\alpha_H / \\iota_\\xi\\alpha</code> restricted to the fibre <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_p</code>. On the affine chart <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">v_2 \\neq 0</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">z</code> generates <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}[z]</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/vertex-operator-affine-coordinate.md","heading":"Remark","number":"13.10.4"}
